<P>&#9;"I don’t know."</P><br><P>&#9;"How you kill it?"</P><br><P>&#9;"I don’t know…my bow, or my sword."</P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher laughed, "You die like a fool then. Everr rraid Blackburrow? Everr fight gnollz?"</P><br><P>&#9;"I have fought a gnoll."</P><br><P>&#9;"NO. Have you fought <B>in</B> Blackburrow!? Not one-gnoll hunting. Twenty gnollz! Fourty gnollz! You are a pup! You must trravel. You muzt learrn many thingz—thingz you not even know arre therre to learrn. To fight thiz thing you must be a <B><I>Grreat Rraiderr</B></I>!"</P><br><P>&#9;This last bit he almost shouted…err…howled. Gnasher certainly got emotional when he talked about raiders and raiding. It was a gnoll thing, I suppose.</P><br><P>&#9;I nodded. He was right. I had felt it back in Qeynos. I needed to travel. I knew nothing of the world beyond Qeynos. I had heard of the Barbarians of the Everfrost Peaks and even seen them in Qeynos. And the Erudites I had also seen, but only from a great distance. It was time to expand my hunting grounds.</P><br><P>&#9;"I was thinking of going to hunt in the Peaks."</P><br><P>&#9;Gnasher leaned back and smiled his snarling smile, "Bewarre, Eshkin. The rroad is the best of beerr! Once you set yourr pawz in motion….might be harrd to stop! And it will be harrderr life sometimez than you think."</P><br><P>&#9;I smiled, "It’s just up to the Peaks, Gnasher. How hard could it be?"</P><br><P></P><br><CENTER>***</CENTER>         <br>
